{"profiles":[{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Sapoyoas","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Sapayoa","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Sapayoa Hartert, 1903","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2492882},"ottId":29742,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Sapayoa","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The sapayoa or broad-billed sapayoa (Sapayoa aenigma) is a suboscine passerine bird found Colombia, Ecuador, and Panama.","revisionId":1374680459,"title":"Sapayoa","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sapayoa","wikidataId":"Q1090032"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Colombian Woolly Monkey","source":"Mammal Species of the World"},{"language":"en","name":"Brown Woolly Monkey","source":"Integrated Taxonomic Information System (ITIS)"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Lagothrix lugens","confidence":98,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Lagothrix lugens Elliot, 1907","status":"SYNONYM","usageKey":4267241},"ottId":57134,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Lagothrix lugens","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Colombian woolly monkey (Lagothrix lagothricha lugens) is a critically endangered subspecies of the common woolly monkey from Colombia. It was initially thought to be a subspecies of the common woolly monkey (L. lagothricha), but was later reclassified as its own species.","revisionId":1313869055,"title":"Colombian woolly monkey","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colombian_woolly_monkey","wikidataId":"Q123049590"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Bornean White-bearded Gibbon","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Bornean Agile Gibbon","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Hylobates albibarbis","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Hylobates albibarbis Lyon, 1911","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":5707402},"ottId":96942,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Hylobates albibarbis","synonyms":["Hylobates agilis albibarbis","Hylobates cinereus albibarbis","Hylobates muelleri albibarbis"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Bornean white-bearded gibbon (Hylobates albibarbis), also known as the Bornean agile gibbon or southern gibbon, is a species of gibbon endemic to southern Borneo. It is an endangered species, due to the ongoing logging of tropical forests between the Kapuas and Barito rivers.","revisionId":1356938983,"title":"Bornean white-bearded gibbon","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bornean_white-bearded_gibbon","wikidataId":"Q1721268"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Viridiplantae","source":"Wikipedia"}],"ottId":361838,"scientificName":"Chloroplastida","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Viridiplantae (New Latin for \"green plants\"), also known as kingdom Plantae sensu stricto (\"plants in a narrow sense\"), is a clade of mostly autotrophic eukaryotes that constitutes the largest group within the predominantly photosynthetic superclade Archaeplastida, with around half a million known species that include all green algae and land plants (embryophytes, which evolved from freshwater green algae known as streptophytes). They are important primary producers in both aquatic (marine and freshwater) and terrestrial ecosystems, and are significant contributors to the Earth's oxygen, carbon and water cycles.","revisionId":1374857215,"title":"Viridiplantae","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viridiplantae","wikidataId":"Q11973077"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Blue-bellied parrot","source":"Wikipedia"}],"ottId":393390,"scientificName":"Triclaria","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The blue-bellied parrot or purple-bellied parrot (Triclaria malachitacea) is the only species in its genus. It is generally considered endemic to the humid Atlantic Forest of southeastern Brazil, but there are two unconfirmed records from Misiones in Argentina.","revisionId":1352365970,"title":"Blue-bellied parrot","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue-bellied_parrot","wikidataId":"Q620349"}},{"commonNames":[{"languag